# Key scale rate 0 to 3 at blocks 0 to 7, one block per segment, on four
# channels (one per KSR value) with the same moderate rates, so each segment
# shows how the key code (block plus the derived fifth bit) speeds the
# envelope. The frequency number is chosen so the fifth bit toggles.
# Then the fifth key-code bit, from F11-F8 of the frequency number: every
# value 0 to 15 at block 3 with KSR 3 and a detune, so the bit shows in both
# the rates and the detune.
